KG42.register("rules-8312febaf448b45a3d5c84d4",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R014","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R014","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The uniform local clearing price determines the common buyer payment and seller receipt rate, kB_γ^P + (1 - k)S_γ^P. Scope: All winning participants in a uniform k-DA local auction interval. Condition: γ is the largest breakeven index satisfying B_γ^P ≥ S_γ^P.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R014-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"All winning participants in a uniform k-DA local auction interval.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta_k","symbol":"k","meaning":"Predetermined constant of the k-Double Auction, fixed in the closed interval [0, 1], that weights the breakeven bid and ask prices in the uniform clearing/payment price kB_\\gamma^P + (1 - k)S_\\gamma^P. The [0, 1] interval is stated in the paper's k-DA definition (Section 2.1), the same mechanism family as Uniform k-DA (v141-a-M02); the constant's use in the formula is quoted in v141-b-g01-ev-04.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"predetermined constant in the closed interval [0, 1]"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_B_gamma","symbol":"B_\\gamma^P","meaning":"Bid price at the largest breakeven index \\gamma; the marginal buyer bid price that enters the uniform clearing price and the common payment rate.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["\\gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_S_gamma","symbol":"S_\\gamma^P","meaning":"Ask price at the largest breakeven index \\gamma; the marginal seller ask price that enters the uniform clearing price and the common receipt rate.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["\\gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_gamma","symbol":"\\gamma","meaning":"Largest breakeven index of the naturally ordered offers, defined by B_\\gamma^P \\geq S_\\gamma^P, that fixes the marginal bid and ask prices used to compute the uniform payment/receipt rate. In the settlement stage this index is a given (fixed) quantity.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"largest breakeven index satisfying B_\\gamma^P \\geq S_\\gamma^P"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R014-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The uniform local clearing price determines the common buyer payment and seller receipt rate, kB_γ^P + (1 - k)S_γ^P. Scope: All winning participants in a uniform k-DA local auction interval. Condition: γ is the largest breakeven index satisfying B_γ^P ≥ S_γ^P.","expression":"p^{pay}_\\gamma = p^{rec}_\\gamma = k B_\\gamma^P + (1 - k) S_\\gamma^P","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_k","theta_B_gamma","theta_S_gamma","theta_gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-02","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminatory k-DA where all winning participants trade at the same price. Such market clearing price is figured by first sorting offers according to the natural ordering rule and determining the largest breakeven index $\\gamma$ where $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$. The market clearing price is then calculated as for single-unit auctions where $B_{\\gamma}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma}^P$ are the bid and ask prices at the largest breakeven index, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-04","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Table 1 Auction mechanisms. Uniform k-DA | Price trading buyers pay: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$ | Price trading sellers receive: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The settlement rule computes a uniform payment/receipt rate that is fully determined by the given constant k and the marginal bid/ask prices at the breakeven index. The two supplied evidence items (v141-b-g01-ev-02, v141-b-g01-ev-04) contain no participant design-selection or operational decision that is free at the settlement stage, so no x variable is declared for this rule (this does not assert that the source lacks variables elsewhere, e.g. in bidding).","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-clearing","v141-a-M02-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-04","quote":"Uniform k-DA | Price trading buyers pay: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$ | Price trading sellers receive: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-02","quote":"Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminatory k-DA where all winning participants trade at the same price. Such market clearing price is figured by first sorting offers according to the natural ordering rule and determining the largest breakeven index $\\gamma$ where $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e68b1a0dac234605682f13d8445195105dec8d7bcbbf0fd3fa89e8710002fd4e","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The uniform k-DA settlement rule is formalized as a source-faithful payment formula. Evidence v141-b-g01-ev-04 (Table 1) states verbatim that for Uniform k-DA the price trading buyers pay and the price trading sellers receive are both $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$, and v141-b-g01-ev-02 defines $\\gamma$ as the largest breakeven index with $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$ and identifies $B_{\\gamma}^P$, $S_{\\gamma}^P$ as the bid and ask prices at that index. Constraint C001 therefore carries the expression p^{pay}_\\gamma = p^{rec}_\\gamma = k B_\\gamma^P + (1 - k) S_\\gamma^P with formalization_origin=source. The frozen nodes pricing.local and settlement.payment and edge v141-c-R014-E001 (pricing.local -> settlement.payment, type links) exactly represent the transfer from the uniform clearing price to the common buyer-payment/seller-receipt rate, so the graph can represent the source formula and no revision is required. No x variable is declared: the settlement stage contains no free design or operational decision, because the rate is a deterministic function of the given constant k and the marginal bid/ask prices at the breakeven index. Parameter k is the prior k-DA constant; the closed interval [0, 1] and the domains/units of B_\\gamma^P and S_\\gamma^P are not contained in the two supplied quotations, so their units are left null. NOTE: this experiment performs no B source audit; both supporting evidence items remain source_status=unverified, so this formalization is provisional and must not be reported as source-audited.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R014-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R014-E001"],"rationale":"C001 formalizes the uniform clearing price (pricing.local) being turned into the common buyer-payment/seller-receipt rate applied at settlement (settlement.payment); this is exactly the pricing.local -> settlement.payment 'links' relation encoded by edge v141-c-R014-E001, and both member nodes are the constraint's declared members."},{"object_id":"theta_k","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R014-E001"],"rationale":"The prior k-DA constant k weights B_\\gamma^P and S_\\gamma^P both in the uniform clearing price formed at pricing.local and in the settled payment/receipt rate at settlement.payment, so it is carried across edge E001 between the two nodes."},{"object_id":"theta_B_gamma","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R014-E001"],"rationale":"B_\\gamma^P is the marginal bid price that both sets the uniform price at pricing.local and enters the settled payment rate at settlement.payment via edge E001."},{"object_id":"theta_S_gamma","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R014-E001"],"rationale":"S_\\gamma^P is the marginal ask price that both sets the uniform price at pricing.local and enters the settled receipt rate at settlement.payment via edge E001."},{"object_id":"theta_gamma","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R014-E001"],"rationale":"\\gamma indexes the largest breakeven bid/ask pair whose prices at pricing.local define the uniform rate that is passed to settlement.payment across edge E001."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
